The torque is $\tau = nIAB\sin\theta$, so the maximum torque can be increased by any two of:
- increasing the number of turns of wire in the coil ($n$);
- increasing the current in the coil ($I$), e.g. using a higher-voltage supply;
- increasing the area of the coil ($A$);
- increasing the magnetic field strength ($B$), e.g. using stronger magnets.
